    62	## What the author owns
    63	
    64	The drill's details and Vastin's mistakes in it. Exactly how the pack moves on ice. How long the scouting takes. The spring's light and wind. The order in which the three readers find things. How Oryn prices each of them, and the fork's last fire. Whether Vastin's three reflexes come in one scene or across the halt.
    65	
    66	## Where we leave pressure
    67	
    68	A city stands on a bluff ahead, with three walls in tiers and a light on its crown. A healer's term is written in the log. A man on a stick has learned one sentence from a defector, and a boy carries a date he will not write down. Five people and a marshal walk toward the first registry Cael has ever gone to on purpose.

