   274	### 7.2 Front-loaded teaching (owner formula §4)
   275	
   276	Target ≈58 progression-vocabulary hits per 10k words overall (≈1,740 over 300k), front-loaded about 1.7×: **first third ≈82 per 10k (≈820 hits), middle ≈43 (≈430), last ≈49 (≈490).** The first third does most of the teaching:
   277	- The cold-term inventory and practice [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] (fragment names, costs, the seal, "deployment notes").
   278	- The board's ranking (eleventh; Teague's four at the top; "the board doesn't ask what a crew was").
   279	- Tiers and Paths in Teague's crew, in Vastin, and in Treswick's machinery (Copper/Iron/Bronze/Silver; passes; tier gates; the smith's two forges; the provision's columns).
   280	- Iron Wall's first showing; the records' grade; the reading inward.
   281	
   282	After the first third, progression language surfaces at turning points: the three notices, the grade, the court's line.
   283	**Measurement caution (as OWNER-DECISIONS #14):** the last third carries **grade vocabulary** (first-, second- and third-tier; the mark; the stroke and bar). Counted as progression vocabulary, it inflates the closing third. Report two counts at each review, with and without grade/taxonomy terms.
   284	
   285	### 7.3 Development cadence (owner formula §5)
   286	
   287	- **Cael:** about 4.5 realization/decision beats per 10k words, ≈135 across the book, spread evenly with a slight middle bump (≈42 / 48 / 45). That is about 15 per movement, so roughly one every 2,200 words.
   288	- **Supporting cast:** many small beats each (§3.D), 0.1–0.7 per 10k per person. No single deuteragonist takes the budget. Karis and Vastin run highest (≈14 each across the book); Pike and the young one run lowest.
   289	
   290	### 7.4 Prose and rhythm targets (formula §2–3, §8–9; measured after each movement with `tools/formula_metrics.py`)
   291	
   292	**Source baseline** (measured 2026-10-01 over all 24 chapters):
   293	
   294	| Metric | Source | Target |
   295	|---|---|---|
   296	| Sentence mean | 21.3 | 14.6 |
   297	| Sentence median | 8 | 11 |
   298	| Spread (sd) | 27.2 | ~26 |
   299	| Sentences ≤5 words | 39.3% | 27.7% |
   300	| Sentences ≥40 words | **19.1%** | 3.3% |
   301	| Paragraph median | **51** | ~18 |
   302	| Paragraph mean | 66.4 | ~26.8 |
   303	| Words per scene | 808 | ~950 |
