   306	| FK grade | 6.7 | 6.8 |
   307	
   308	The source's signature is the accumulating catalogue sentence, chained with "and … and … because …". That produces both the 19% of sentences over forty words and the paragraphs of fifty-plus words, while very short beats pull the median and the Flesch score up. **For this edition:**
   309	- Break the catalogue chains into well-built compound and complex sentences of 12–25 words.
   310	- Keep a few deliberate forty-plus sentences per chapter where accumulation is the effect, such as an inventory or a crossing.
   311	- Bring paragraphs down toward a median of 18 by ending the paragraph when the thought turns.
   312	- Keep short punch sentences for landings, not as default (EDITION_BRIEF rhythm calibration).
   313	- Hold a scene break roughly every 950 words.
   314	- Drop dialogue tags where the speaker is clear.
   315	- Adverbs and fillers are to taste: do not chase "that".
   316	
   317	**Logs are exempt from the chain-breaking only where §10 fixes their text.**
