   421	| The Arbiter system is the Architect's live infrastructure | 9 | Plants only: "Behaves as device. Cannot be."; "no key"; the lamps finding on its own page; the dark Arbiter unchanged. Never join the leaf to the sigils. No *terminal / circuit / infrastructure*. The Arbiter never speaks. |
   422	| Cael is a recurrence (the tomb; the un-bound practitioner's record) | 9 | Never say "recurrence". No tomb, no hint of one. "The same kind of made" and "the pattern" are the ceiling. The third sentence stays unwritten. |
   423	| The court's name | 9 | "The court", lowercase, descriptive only. Never "the Court", never "Still Court". |
