   241	- **The completion report (repaired to Book 7).** It carries the Fallow posting's head, a town on no registry map and a board; **"where a crew's name should have been there were five strokes, and after the strokes a count, which was six."** No names. It reached Vastin as a courtesy copy with no routing note; it took him the cold term to find the file that it belonged to, "which stands in no register". He does not know who had the abstracts held, and looked. Whether the copy was sent to him on purpose is Seln's question, left open.
   242	- **The flat (repaired):** a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather, "as broad as a man's shoulders and no thicker than two fingers", stamped *BY SEAT COURIER. BY HAND.*; six rows, a year to a row, the newest uppermost, each in a tape; a pocket in the lid. **The abstracts:** printed forms; four signs and a number at the head (the Stair's sheet has the dead surveyor's four signs and thirty-two); a column for the day in the office's reckoning; a measure given in lengths, knots and strides; and a narrow right-hand column whose printed head says that it is for **the anomaly**. **In every clerk's hand, in every one of six years, that column holds the single word *Total*, and nobody has written a second word beside it.** There is no figure and no sum. Karis counts more than four different groups of signs in the newest row, on her fingers, and will not say a number until she has checked it in daylight. No sheets are counted.
   243	- **The page (repaired): a copy.** One sheet of the house's plain desk paper, folded twice, in Vastin's own square upright hand, in fresh ink. He copied the line "from a record that is older than the section it is filed in, in a room where I had the right to read and no right to copy", with the word and the place "exactly as they are written there, letter for letter", and the schedule of housings round it (a number, a date of setting and a mender's mark to each) to show where the line falls. He read the pages on both sides and did not copy them. **No cut edge, no blade, no inquiry, and no prompt from the ninth fragment.**
   244	- **The sheet (repaired):** thin stock, newer than the rest, a printed head, "a quick sloping hand"; a technician's return ("When a man who services the stations finds a thing that he was not sent to find, he is bound to write it up on such a sheet, on the day, and send it in"). **The office had filed it with the surveys, at the end of the second row; Vastin carried it in the lid to keep it dry; Karis has laid it back at the foot of the second row.** Its date is a registry year and a day in it, in the office's reckoning; **no figures are printed anywhere.** The bar is as broad as a thumb, laid on both sides, cracked in drying; Vastin has seen such a bar "on perhaps a dozen papers in forty years" and never with initials. He does not know which classification event is meant.
   245	- **Karis's receipt (repaired), 12:173:** *Received of Vastin, at Lowmarch, day two hundred and seventy-seven past the Line: one courier's flat, holding six rows of abstracts in their tapes, one row looked through and no sheet counted; one broker's report; one page, copied by him from a register; one technician's sheet, copied by me this night and laid back in the second row. Read in part. Understood in no part. — K.*
   246	- **Names given at the board (ch10):** the six tell Vastin their names; he had Cael's and Karis's from paper and "took some trouble never to learn" the others. Seln gives his.
   247	- **Roles (all unnamed):** the courier with the cut hat-brim and the old carter with pale eyes (both from Book 7's road); the boy with a tally stick on the western landing; the landing broker and his clerk; the man with the ledger who carries the bag; the passengers; the woman with the loaves; the keeper.
   248	
   249	### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
   250	**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and seventy-seventh day past the Line**, at Lowmarch. Days on the page: 271, 272, 273, 275, 276, 277; Vastin's window, 265–276. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page.
   251	
   252	**Where everyone is.** Seven under the lower inn's roof: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln; Oryn, who is on her road and at her bench by first light; and **Vastin, in the loft over the tap, at a copper a night**, who is on nobody's sheet and has asked for nothing but a bed. Teague's five are at the upper inn, with forty sacks of salt on the bank. The brown mule is in the ferryman's shed.
   253	
   254	**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: thirty** (the read on the ground at the landing, the 277th). Shadow used twice in all and shut; held at dusk on the 272nd and the 277th. Anchor's counted uses still two. Tide: Oryn twice, himself three times, nobody else; he did not ask to read the knee. **The still place** has not been read, touched or named. He has not touched the cord or either brass edge for a hundred and nine days; the ruling is *hold*. His near sight went at the landing and was back for print by the afternoon. **He has not ruled.** He will say it "at the plank in the morning, in daylight" and ask for hands. He has not touched the copied page; his hand lay a hand's width from it for the whole of a lamp. **He has not read the technician's date**: he was at the table's far end; he knows that it is a registry year and a day, and that it is the line at which Seln stopped; he chose not to go up the table and read it. He lost the bout to Lira, two touches to three. He has written to Ephram. He kept back his own question to Vastin (why the second reading was declined). He has told Vastin nothing of what he carries.
   255	
   256	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Left arm: the eighth day out of the wool on the 273rd. It told her once, in the bout, and she did not stop.** It is slow; it ached after rain. She did not fall on it. Right ankle sound in the great boot. Her certificate is in her coat. She still has Oryn's crossbow and its one bolt (not mentioned in these chapters). She sat last at the table; she asked "Why us." and "What follows you,"; she read the technician's sheet aloud, without its figures.
   257	
   258	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No declaration; no grey at the landing. **Right shoulder still in the older healer's webbing**; she pressed the knot on the 272nd and went away. He shored the post with a timber on the left shoulder. He has the purse; a hundred and eighteen. He roped the three boxes for carrying on the night of the 277th.
   259	
   260	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Her case stands "not by a line" altered. She holds, received and receipted: **the flat, with six rows in their tapes (one row looked through; no sheet counted) and the technician's sheet laid back at the foot of the second row; the broker's completion report; Vastin's copied page**, which lies on its oilcloth at the bare end of her table; and **her own exact copy of the technician's sheet**, with the office's date figures as they stand, a ruled box and *not read* in it, and a note of where the sheet lies. She has said that the word on the page is a title and not a name, that she has never met it in any stratum, and nothing more. She has said "More than four" and no number. She has seen *Total* in the anomaly column on every sheet she turned, in the newest row and the oldest. She cannot read the index; it is an office's index now and not only the dead man's. She has connected nothing to anything. She keeps the lamp.
   261	
   262	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. He has spoken with Vastin for the first time (the doorway) and has given him his name. He has stopped his count at **forty-seven notches on the second wand (a hundred and forty-seven days)** and laid the wand on Karis's table. **He went still when Karis's pencil came to the date on the technician's sheet**, and said only "I have read it." He has taught nobody anything. He thinks the completion report may have been sent to Vastin on purpose and cannot tell. **The case is on him, shut.**
   263	
   264	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. A bench under the eave since the 272nd. She saw the bout and said nothing. She has not asked about the knee, and Vastin has offered it to nobody; she seconded Karis's order to bed with one line about the stairs. **She has not read Cael.** She has shut her mouth three times on the same sentence. She did not sit on the stool. She does not know that Seln is Shadow's source.
   265	
   266	**Vastin.** No office, no seal, no rank; he left the seal in a tray "some months" ago and walked three hundred miles. **No age is stated.** A bad knee; raw hands; a left hand that will not lie flat. **No Iron Wall has been shown or named.** He has handed over three things in his own order and holds Karis's receipt in his coat. He has said: that he holds no office and has no sanction; that the layer cannot be opened ("There is no key"), on the authority of the office's own page; that the one line which should name its maker cites a title and sends its reader to Treswick's lower archive (his own copy of it); that nothing of his follows him and the Stair's rim is not his; that the pending paper is unchanged; why he did not take it to a council. He knows the six by name. **He does not know** the mechanism, what Cael carries, the instruments' behaviour in Cael's hand, Karis's case or the sites (beyond hearing Brom say "four on the hide" and Lira name the Stair), who held the abstracts, which classification event the sheet means, or what is under the bar. He has not weighed the sheet's date. He has not read the flat's last row through, and nothing has been said of a directive or an objection. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. He was sent to bed, began to argue twice, took four stairs fast and the rest slowly; whether that was the order or the knee is not settled.
   267	
   268	**Teague and his crew.** The wrist is unbound; he has tried it on nothing. He asked "When?" and was told "I don't know." His term holds without a day in it. The tall man drove the wedge at the post and grounded his spear for Lira; he, the bow and the older healer have said nothing to the six. Teague looked at Vastin's hands a stride longer than a crew looks, and said nothing. Nobody in his crew is named. He knows nothing of the mechanism or of what was said at the table.
   269	
   270	**Pike's book and the cloth.** **Eleven lines.** The season line's number still blank. **Eleventh on the new cloth**, painted on the 272nd. Vastin is "nothing yet" and is not entered. Oryn is on no slip.
   271	
   272	**Objects and money.** **A hundred and eighteen marks in hand**, unchanged. The reserve sealed. Owed: **sixty yards of four-strand rope** to the ferryman (the cordage is on the western landing; his one hauling rope has two yarns gone). **The hurdle is paid.** **The letter to Ephram is sent.** The three boxes are at the hearth's end, roped. Stake thirty-two has still never been driven. On Karis's table: the flat (the sheet inside it), the broker's paper beside it, Seln's wand beside that, and the copied page at the far end.
   273	
   274	**The Quieting, as known.** Unchanged in the field. On paper: an office has surveyed the sites for six years by cord, has classed each under four signs, and has written one word, *Total*, in its anomaly column every time; its abstracts were held where nobody received them; the places are more than four.
   275	
   276	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before. The anomaly of the cord and the edges: the six. Karis's case: the six. What Vastin brought: the six and Vastin. Nobody has said who made the layer, or why, or what is running in it. Nobody has connected the sheet's date to anybody; only Seln has reacted to it, and only Cael has noticed that it was the date.
   277	
   278	**Words said aloud for the first time.** *Vastin* (Seln, at the landing). *Treswick* by Vastin, at noon, from the other side. On paper only, and said by nobody: the title on the page. Not said aloud by anybody in chapters 10–12: *west*.
   279	
   280	**Open threads.** A ruling to be given at the plank in the morning. A page that Cael has not touched. A date that stopped Seln and that Cael has not read. A bar with something under it. A count that Karis has not checked. A paper that came to a desk with no routing note. A sentence that a healer has swallowed three times. A knee that nobody has asked about. A man in a loft with a receipt and nothing to do. A rope on the wrong bank. A captain's term with no day in it. A question that Cael kept.
   281	
   282	### Next-movement inheritance (Sol plan audit §8; also written into the next packet)
   283	Packet 003 already carries day 278, the clearance slip, Vastin at the door end and not on the sheet, the silent drill, the cut, the spring, the date sum, the fork and days 279–281 (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:20–38`). Its author must additionally inherit:
