   236	
   237	He turned his back on the mark, and walked.
   238	
   239	Wind had his feet before the first stride was down. It leaned him at the foot of the cut with everything that it had, and he told it no, and found that his own two legs had something to offer in its place: a walk, a little bent, close under the scree, such as a girl on a bench had beaten into him with the two halves of a count. He did not run. A thing that ran on that road would be looked at.
   240	
