     1	# Chapter 15 — The Loudest Thing
     2	
     3	He understood it in the time that it took them to cover the first five strides, and it was far too late to be of use.
     4	
     5	They had learned the road. Nothing that had ever declared at the top of that glass had stayed there. It had gone down the hill backward, with a man hanging on its tailboard and a Path blazing in him, and it had come to rest at the foot; and three times the grey things had run to the head of the cut, and found the sound already sixty strides below them. They did not go any longer to where a declaration was made. They went to where it ended.
     6	
