    43	The thing did not give by the breadth of a hair. It did not ring, or shake; the frost that lay on it never stirred. The hound went back up the hill on its side, with all four legs working, and the second went into it, and the third into the second. Behind those the rest were braking with everything that they had, sliding on their haunches down the glass. One after another they came against that face in a slither of grey bodies, and were stopped.
    44	
    45	Eight of them had come at it running, and not one had got through. It held.
    46	
    47	Cael had seen Paths used on floors for half his life. He had seen fire run between nine points, and a girl leave one place and arrive in another, and a Gold lay the air down in lanes; and every one of those had been a thing that went out and did something. This did nothing whatever. It was a plane, as flat as a rule and as thin as a thought. It had been drawn on the ground and stood on end. It kept the ground's own refusal to be walked through, and it would have been all one to it whether a moth struck it or a cart.
