+# Source-distance audit — Movement 003
+
+Independent side-by-side read of source chapters 4–6 against edition chapters 13–19. This is a source-distance review, not a cold-reader review. I excluded every unit identified in `protected-patterns.txt`, every protected unit in `BOOK_MAP.md` §10, and every line quoted or supplied in `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md`. I also treated the packet and map as plan evidence: required facts, scene events, and choreography are not counted where the manuscript gives them a new telling.
+
+The requested calibrated probe reported a 2% skeleton rate and a 15% close rate. Its strongest pairs were overwhelmingly protected dialogue/log text or common constructions. In particular, the nominally dense chapter 18, scene 5 is made dense by the protected Karis/Cleon close; it is not an author-prose source-distance failure. The three findings below come from the side-by-side read.
+
+## 1. Verdict
+
+**Three genuine tracked passages in the movement.** Each is a local sentence-level inheritance; no scene is densely tracked.
+
+| Chapter | Scene 1 | Scene 2 | Scene 3 | Scene 4 | Scene 5 | Chapter total |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| 13 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** |
+| 14 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** |
+| 15 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** |
+| 16 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** |
+| 17 | 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **1** |
+| 18 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 | **1** |
+| 19 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **1** |
+| **Movement** |  |  |  |  |  | **3** |
+
+Scene numbers follow the manuscript's `---` divisions; scene 1 is the material before the first divider.
+
+## 2. Tracked passages
+
+| chapter:line | Manuscript opening words | Source sentence followed | Kind |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `chapter-17.md:89` | “Her finger lay beside the ruled space, not on it.” | `books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-05.md:61` — “Her finger above a sheet in the first row — the Ring — not on it.” | near-verbatim |
+| `chapter-18.md:139` | “It was the first thing since he had learned to hold a pencil…” | `books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-05.md:103` — “There was a thing between the two of them now…” | varied |
+| `chapter-19.md:33` | “It doesn't matter which; they're all one city, with different rivers.” | `books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-06.md:25` — “I've been in a city. I was certified in one. I'll not say which…” | near-verbatim |
+
+### Beat chains to break
+
+- **17:89:** The source places Karis's finger near documentary evidence and immediately emphasizes that it is above, not touching, the sheet. The manuscript moves the gesture to the ruled remark but keeps the same near-evidence → explicit non-contact sequence and much of the sentence frame. Break it by letting the pencil or a pebble locate the remark, by having her touch and then withdraw, or by putting the interpretation before any physical gesture.
+
+- **18:139:** The source names the knowledge as the first thing Cael has possessed without writing down, then lets him discover that he can carry it. The manuscript keeps unprecedented unrecorded knowledge → discovery of capacity/ease in the same order, changing possession/carrying into knowing/not entering and fear at its ease. Break it by opening on his fear at the blank line, returning the book first, and only later contrasting this choice with his lifelong habit of entry.
+
+- **19:33:** The source declines to identify the city, says the particular city does not matter, and collapses all cities into one healer's experience. The manuscript keeps does-not-matter-which → all-one-city in the same words and order, adding “different rivers.” Break it by entering through the patient's tier column or the untiered woman's bed, then reveal only afterward that Oryn refuses to name the city because the system, not the place, is the point.
+
+No other passage met the threshold. The slip, road doctrine, cut terrain and positions, Iron Wall mechanics, burst/lock/heap sequence, costs, spring readings, short row and placed sheet, Kindling-date sum, Seln's lesson, fork terms, patient pricing, departure, and first view of Treswick all follow required plan events. Their manuscript staging and sentence development are new except for protected wording and the three local sentences above.
+
+## 3. Dense-scene guidance
